# Example environment configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. NEVER commit real credentials, a real database URL, or a
# password hash. Every value below is a placeholder.
#
# Nothing in this project auto-loads .env - there is no python-dotenv
# dependency. Export the variables yourself, or let your platform inject them:
#
#   PowerShell   $env:DATABASE_URL = "sqlite-local"
#   bash         export DATABASE_URL=""
#   Docker       docker run --env-file .env ...
#   Render       Dashboard -> Environment
#   Streamlit    .streamlit/secrets.toml (see .streamlit/secrets.toml.example)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inference logging database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by inference_db.py, from the environment first and then from Streamlit
# secrets. Leave it EMPTY or unset to use the local SQLite file at
# data/inference_logs.db, which is created automatically and is gitignored.
#
# Only a postgresql:// or postgres:// value switches the app to PostgreSQL. The
# public app and the admin dashboard must share the same URL for the admin
# dashboard to see the inference logs written by the public app.
#
# Example shape only - host, user and password below are not real:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DBNAME?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin dashboard bootstrap credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by admin_auth.ensure_default_admin(), which admin_app.py calls to seed
# admin_users.json the first time the dashboard starts. Passwords are stored as
# a PBKDF2-SHA256 hash plus a salt; the plaintext is never written to disk.
#
# SECURITY NOTE: if these are unset, the code currently falls back to a
# well-known built-in default and seeds an admin account automatically. Always
# set both here. Redesigning that default-admin behaviour is a separate,
# pending security task - this file only documents safe configuration.
#
# Minimum password length is 8 characters. Replace the placeholder before use.
ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not application configuration - listed so the set is complete
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL  bilayered_neural.py SETS this itself ('2') to quieten
#                       TensorFlow. It is never read as configuration, so you
#                       do not need to provide it.
# PORT                  Injected by Render and used in render.yaml start
#                       commands. Do not set it locally.
# PYTHON_VERSION        Build-time platform setting in render.yaml, not a
#                       runtime variable. Pinned to the canonical tested
#                       version there.
# PYTHONUNBUFFERED      Set by the Dockerfile for the container runtime.
# PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE
#                       Set by the Dockerfile for the container runtime.
